ce, where the circuit need not be able to follow; this experiment does not separate the size of the realised steps from the curvature of the set of policies the circuit can reach as causes of the remaining gap.",
  "Over a damping ladder, HQ-Fisher − TAN at κ = 0.01 in the 33 retained two-layer units was δ = 10⁻⁶: −6.19 [−8.87, −3.51]; δ = 10⁻⁴: −6.33 [−8.85, −3.80]; δ = 10⁻²: −5.96 [−8.34, −3.59]; δ = 1: −5.49 [−8.13, −2.86] (× 10⁻⁵; δ = 10⁻⁶ is the B1 setting); at this KL, the shortfall of the circuit-realised step is therefore not specific to near-zero damping. Outside this primary cell the difference was unresolved for δ = 1 at κ = 0.001 in the three-layer stratum (−0.28 [−0.68, +0.12]) and for the plain step at κ = 0.001 in the three-layer stratum (+0.08 [−0.36, +0.53]). Appendix A lists every arm."
